From 11563ac4fd011000a77998496215336689e93a21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gaius Mulley <gaiusmod2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH] PR modula2/125129: Many tests fail to link on FreeBSD

This patch combines a series of patches starting with the above
title.  The squashing contains all the fixup patches for the original
large patch.  The fixups detect whether we have a Python3 interpreter
and use posix shell commands.

Not all targets have csin[l], ccos[l] and ctan[l].  On such systems
the ISO libraries should be pruned thus allowing compile time failures
for source which explicitly requests these intrinsics rather than universally
fail on linking.  This patch introduces a new tool mktargetsrc which
will generate target versions of the Modula-2 libraries.  The patch also
introduces -fdump-builtins (an internal option) which is used
by mktargetsrc.  mktargetsrc replaces makeSystem and mktargetsrc improves
the formatting of the autogenerated SYSTEM.def files.
Bootstrapped on x86_64 Debian and FreeBSD15 and all regression tests pass.

